To write a Fibonacci number function in Rust, you can use an iterative approach which is efficient and avoids the overhead of recursion. Here's a simple implementation:

```rust
fn fibonacci(n: u32) -> u32 {
    let mut a = 0;
    let mut b = 1;
    for _ in 0..n {
        let temp = a;
        a = b;
        b = temp + b;
    }
    a
}
```

This function calculates the nth Fibonacci number. It uses two mutable variables to keep track of the last two numbers in the sequence and iterates n times to compute the result.
